{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/sec-q-harmonic-analysis-intro","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"sec:q-harmonic-analysis-intro","kind":"prose","text":"q-harmonic-analysis-intro.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"sec:q-harmonic-analysis-intro\"></a><p>We build heat-flow, Laplace, Fourier, and resolvent calculus on top of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed operators. The framework organises around the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-shuffle Hopf algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{H}_q</code> and its grouplikes <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\exp_q, \\log_q, \\mathrm{Li}_2^q</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-analysis-intro.md","heading":""}
